To configure an AWS IAM policy to grant access to a specific S3 bucket, while denying access to all other buckets, I would use the `arn:aws:s3:::bucket-name` syntax to specify the bucket name. For example:
```bash
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "AllowAccessToSpecificBucket",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::example-bucket"
    }
  ]
}
```
This policy would grant access to the specific S3 bucket, while denying access to all other buckets.

